                        "glosses": [
                            "Impossible to cross."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ad59013-fe75-49e1-841e-478ae350575b",
                                "sense_id": "483042d9-c56d-3700-aa0a-de062916c28d",
                                "text": "There is what appears under normal circumstances to be an uncrossable boundary, a total barrier."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "94a9b954-e03c-4e8a-9a07-e5f9b90dd5b9",
                                "sense_id": "483042d9-c56d-3700-aa0a-de062916c28d",
                                "text": "And it’s brilliantly stitched together by motifs of chrysalises and movies and by a joyous abundance of metaphor and simile: “the ding of a bicycle bell like struck crystal”; a woman “talking for much of the day in a steady soft uncrossable stream.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db462961-1a57-4c08-9ecb-5a44bd3cc025",
                                "sense_id": "483042d9-c56d-3700-aa0a-de062916c28d",
                                "text": "There are very few bridges on the footpaths in Skye and even short periods of heavy rain can cause rivers to rise rapidly, often making them uncrossable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c55a2443-c18c-4302-b8f6-f2fd311fc3b1",
                                "sense_id": "483042d9-c56d-3700-aa0a-de062916c28d",
                                "text": "There are two Underground stations. That serving the District and Piccadilly is on one side of an uncrossable road called Hammersmith Broadway; that serving the Hammersmith & City is on the other side. Whichever exit you emerge from, at whichever station, you are immediately lost."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
